      "text": "To find the area of a square, we need to use the formula for the area of a square:\nArea = side * side = side^2\n\nWe know that the perimeter of a square is 32 ft, so to find the side of the square, we need to divide the perimeter by 4 because all four sides of a square have the same length.\nSide = Perimeter / 4 = 32 ft / 4 = 8 ft\n\nNow that we know the side of the square is 8 ft, we can find the area by squaring the side length:\nArea = side^2 = 8 ft * 8 ft = 64 square ft\n\nTherefore, the area of the square with a perimeter of 32 ft is \\boxed{64}.",
