      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a square, we need to find its side length. The perimeter of a square is the sum of the lengths of all its sides. For a square with side length s, the perimeter is 4s.\n\nSo we have the equation:\n\n4s = 32\n\nTo solve for s, we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n\ns = 32 / 4\n\ns = 8\n\nNow that we know the side length is 8, we can find the area of the square:\n\nArea = side length * side length\n\nArea = 8 * 8\n\nArea = 64 square feet\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\boxed{64} square feet.",
